WEBVTT

00:00:01.150 --> 00:00:04.950
On a building project,
different teams model the structure,

00:00:04.951 --> 00:00:07.884
the ducts, the pipes
and the cable trays separately.

00:00:08.334 --> 00:00:10.756
When the models come together,
they collide.

00:00:11.046 --> 00:00:12.859
These are called clashes.

00:00:13.128 --> 00:00:15.775
Finding and fixing them
takes engineers days.

00:00:16.038 --> 00:00:19.171
AI can help,
but it can be confidently wrong.

00:00:20.182 --> 00:00:21.606
This is Iris.

00:00:21.888 --> 00:00:23.260
AI proposes.

00:00:23.404 --> 00:00:24.908
Geometry proves.

00:00:25.016 --> 00:00:26.344
The engineer decides.

00:00:26.866 --> 00:00:28.172
Let's try the sample building.

00:00:29.181 --> 00:00:35.163
Northbank has four models
from different teams, with 1,732 elements.

00:00:35.784 --> 00:00:38.930
Iris finds 464 clashes.

00:00:39.174 --> 00:00:41.863
Live on the cloud,
that takes about 11 seconds.

00:00:42.531 --> 00:00:47.337
Here, the sample replays a saved check
that matches a live run, bit for bit.

00:00:48.345 --> 00:00:50.570
Let's open clash #1.

00:00:50.956 --> 00:00:56.093
A 600×300 supply-air duct runs right
through a transfer girder,

00:00:56.093 --> 00:00:58.056
one metre deep, on Level 02.

00:00:58.171 --> 00:01:00.278
They overlap by 300 mm.

00:01:01.050 --> 00:01:05.141
Iris shows it in 3D,
with three pictures: A, B and C.

00:01:06.497 --> 00:01:08.012
Now, Prepare fixes.

00:01:08.482 --> 00:01:13.184
Gemini 3.8 Flash proposes fixes
that are real edits to the model.

00:01:13.883 --> 00:01:16.519
Then geometry re-checks every one.

00:01:16.671 --> 00:01:20.578
The clash must be gone,
the clearance met, and nothing new hit.

00:01:21.295 --> 00:01:26.363
In this sample, Gemini's saved replies
are replayed, and every check runs again.

00:01:27.389 --> 00:01:28.841
The review queue is ready.

00:01:29.275 --> 00:01:32.777
All 8 clashes got a fix
the geometry verified.

00:01:33.086 --> 00:01:34.569
On the 3 girder clashes,

00:01:34.569 --> 00:01:37.839
the fixes match the human designer's
real revision, exactly.

00:01:38.563 --> 00:01:43.138
The duct rises 400 mm
through the web opening, with 50 mm clear.

00:01:43.683 --> 00:01:48.481
The cable tray rises 250 mm,
and the cold-water pipe 280 mm.

00:01:49.491 --> 00:01:50.750
See it for yourself.

00:01:51.225 --> 00:01:52.833
Before shows the clash.

00:01:53.124 --> 00:01:54.604
After shows the fix.

00:01:54.985 --> 00:01:57.913
Both shows them together,
in the same 3D view.

00:01:58.923 --> 00:02:00.535
The engineer decides.

00:02:00.705 --> 00:02:04.483
Nothing is applied until you press Accept,
with your name on it.

00:02:04.872 --> 00:02:06.498
Or reject it, with a reason.

00:02:06.990 --> 00:02:09.291
Then Iris moves on to the next clash.

00:02:10.301 --> 00:02:13.814
When you're done,
export the report: a PDF,

00:02:13.853 --> 00:02:19.218
and a BCF file that opens in Revit,
Navisworks, Solibri and BIMcollab.

00:02:20.244 --> 00:02:21.575
AI proposes.

00:02:21.847 --> 00:02:23.008
Geometry proves.

00:02:23.387 --> 00:02:25.093
The engineer decides.

00:02:25.363 --> 00:02:30.730
Iris runs on Google Cloud, with Gemini
on Vertex AI, Cloud Run and Firebase.

00:02:31.355 --> 00:02:32.691
Built by Techjays.
